# Wave W17-N (Route 111): dune thorn — a desert thorn tree: a SPARSE pale crown by design (the desert keeps its trees honest — thin grey-green needle mass with the sky showing through, never inflated), one lean trunk, on dune turf (ground baked in). Route 111’s own tree — split from every fat lowland canopy in the fleet by its thinness, which is its identity, and from Route 113’s ash-pale pine by register (thorn scrub, not conifer).
